// count -- kMaxClearSwapCycles=10 (not 120; G14 showed frames can be
// slow, so 120 real presents could take minutes, not what's wanted for a
// bounded diagnostic run) -- with kMaxRuntimeAfterFirstPresentMs raised to
// a genuine SAFETY-NET value (60s) that should essentially never trip
// before the 10-present cap unless something is truly hung, rather than
// being the primary/expected trigger the way 8s was in G14.
//
// iteration-G16, Parte S: G15's real-hardware run hit a CPU FAULT (guest
// executed/jumped into stack data after mciSendStringA("open cdaudio"),
// see winmm_ign.cpp's G16 comment and ignition_boot.cpp's enriched fault
// dump) BEFORE the frame-loop watchdog ever became relevant -- the fault
// is caught at the top level (br.call_va), entirely independent of this
// file's own request_halt() calls. This iteration's explicit instruction
// is to make the frame-loop cycle cap NOT the primary stop trigger, so it
// can't mask/preempt further legitimate guest progress toward wherever
// the real issue is: raised well past anything a bounded diagnostic run
// would realistically reach. kMaxRuntimeAfterFirstPresentMs (60s) remains
// the real safety net, per Part S's "hard safety: 60 sec."
//
// iteration-G28, Parte A/B/T: RETIRED as a halt trigger entirely. G27's
// real-hardware run reached Ignition's own interactive frontend (Loading
// -> Language Selection screen, visually confirmed) and this watchdog then
// killed a game that was genuinely alive and waiting on input --
// FRAME_LOOP_STILL_NO_NEW_GLIDE_CALL / hard_wallclock_cap /
// present_count_cap never fire request_halt() anymore (explicit
// instruction: "no tiene sentido matar la ejecucion porque no aparezca
