// DIRECTLY into two 256-entry-shaped ARGB lookup tables at ds:0x61e720
// and ds:0x61eab4 to compute an explicit flat particle color. This is
// strong, direct disassembly evidence that [esi+0x18] is a **per-
// particle color/material palette index**, not a texture handle, not a
// pointer, and not anything this project's Glide/texture wrapper
// produces. Its valid range (0..255, a plain byte) and its use as a
// literal array index elsewhere in the SAME struct family make an
// invalid/negative value look exactly like an uninitialized-or-expired-
