//      other real Glide type this project has used), not a pointer to a
//      `GuTexMemInfo` or any other dereferenceable struct. There is no
//      real Glide 2.x API contract requiring the game to read fields out
//      of this value -- it is designed to be passed back opaquely into
//      guTexDownloadMipMap/guTexSource, exactly matching this project's
//      existing G39 handle model (0x70000001, ...).
//   2) Direct disassembly of the real allocation call site (0x0044feda:
//      `call 0x468bf2` = guTexAllocateMemory thunk, confirmed since G39)
//      through its return-value handling (0x0044fedf-0x0044fefe): the
//      returned value (moved to esi) is ONLY ever (a) compared against
//      the failure sentinel 0xFFFFFFFF and (b) pushed as an opaque
//      argument to guTexDownloadMipMap (thunk 0x468bec). No
//      `mov eax,[esi+N]`/`mov [esi+N],...`/`cmp [esi+N],...` pattern
//      exists anywhere in this immediate call-and-return sequence --
//      Ignition treats the handle exactly as an opaque token here,
//      matching the real contract. This is Success Case C: the branch
//      condition is UNRELATED to our texture-allocator's return
//      representation.
//
