// -- G65's own proof, reconfirmed here); family_compat=DISABLED for this
// specific pair (0x0045259B/0x004525B2 remain UNTOUCHED by g71_compat_
// predicate -- see CASE6 in g71_selftest()). The real next question this
// opens (deferred to a future iteration, NOT decided here) is what real
// Voodoo hardware/nGlide's own D3D or GL backend actually DOES with a
// NaN-shaped iterated color component such that the game visibly
// continues -- vitaGL/the real Vita GPU may or may not tolerate it the
// same way, and that is a genuinely different question from "what value
// should replace it," which remains unproven and unanswered.
